{
  "summary": "You identify the central safety dilemma, relevant stakeholders and organisational pressures, and reach a defensible no-ship conclusion. To make your case more convincing, correct the failure-rate calculation and Volkswagen account, strengthen evidence-based risk analysis, and make the recommendation’s safety conditions and delivery plan explicit.",
  "next_steps": [
    "In “Discussion: To Ship or Not to Ship,” correct the calculation: 1% of 5,000 servers is 50. Separate the known defect from its likelihood and potential severity, then set evidence-based criteria for any release decision.",
    "In “The Most Ethical Path” and References, correct the Volkswagen example and verify the Engineers Australia code wording and clause numbers. Support key claims with accurate, relevant sources and qualitative or quantitative evidence.",
    "Revise “Recommendation” to state whether Rachel should accept the contract while withholding shipment until defects are resolved, testing is adequate and a safe delivery plan is agreed. Clarify the timeline; add the missing abstract and visuals that support your discussion."
  ],
  "criteria": {
    "C1": "Your Introduction identifies safety, business pressure, professional responsibility and relevant stakeholders, linking the dilemma to engineering organisations and design decisions. This meets the highest rubric level. To strengthen it further, distinguish more clearly how each stakeholder’s interests and risks differ.",
    "C2": "Your Discussion presents arguments for and against shipping, and your conclusion favours not shipping. To reach Very good, assess the trade-offs in greater depth using evidence rather than speculation, and give decision recommendations tailored to several stakeholders.",
    "C3": "Your report’s pro/con structure is easy to follow, and the conclusion draws on safety and business concerns. To reach Very good, build a more compelling evidence-led argument, correct the case-study error, and reconcile the conclusion with the recommendation to accept the contract.",
    "C4": "You include professional guidance and external examples, but the Volkswagen account is inaccurate and the failure-rate calculation is wrong. To reach Very good, verify sources and claims, support arguments with adequate references and qualitative or quantitative evidence, and develop a balanced account of risk.",
    "C5": "Your report has recognisable introduction, body and conclusion sections. To reach Good, add the missing abstract, use visual elements to support the discussion, improve language fluency, and provide a consistent, complete reference list with relevant sources."
  }
}
